# beehiiv

> beehiiv is the newsletter platform built for growth. It provides creators, publishers, and brands with the tools to create, distribute, grow, and monetize newsletters — all in one platform.

The platform serves 130,000+ publishers who have collectively sent over 50 billion emails to 425 million+ unique readers and earned $45M+ through the platform. Plans start free and scale with your audience.

## When to use beehiiv

- Start, write, and send a newsletter, with automations and personalized content. [Newsletter platform](https://www.beehiiv.com/newsletter-platform.md)
- Build a website or link-in-bio page on a custom domain, with AI design help. [Website builder](https://www.beehiiv.com/web-builder.md)
- Host and distribute a podcast alongside a newsletter. [Podcasts](https://www.beehiiv.com/features/podcasts.md)
- Give readers a members-only community, free or behind a paid tier, synced with the newsletter. [Community](https://www.beehiiv.com/features/community.md)
- Grow an audience with referrals, recommendations, and segmentation. [Referral program](https://www.beehiiv.com/features/referral-program.md)
- Earn from an audience with ads, paid subscriptions, and digital products. [Ad Network](https://www.beehiiv.com/ad-network.md), [paid subscriptions](https://www.beehiiv.com/features/premium-subscriptions.md), [digital products](https://www.beehiiv.com/features/digital-products.md)
- Advertise to newsletter readers through the beehiiv Ad Network. [Advertise](https://www.beehiiv.com/i-want-to/advertise.md)
- Run many publications for a media company, with SSO and SCIM. [Enterprise](https://www.beehiiv.com/enterprise.md)
- Move a newsletter from another platform, or compare beehiiv with one. [Migrate](https://www.beehiiv.com/migrate.md), [comparisons](https://www.beehiiv.com/comparisons.md)
- Manage subscribers, posts, and publications in code. [Developers](https://developers.beehiiv.com)

## How agents should use beehiiv

- Quote pricing for a subscriber count with the MCP tool `get_pricing` at `https://www.beehiiv.com/api/mcp`. Do not scrape the HTML slider.
- Help a creator choose Free, Lite, Pro, or Enterprise with `get_pricing` and `pricing_faq`.
- Answer product, feature, or comparison questions from the markdown pages (`*.md`), or with the MCP tools `get_page_markdown` and `compare_with`.
- Call the REST API at `https://api.beehiiv.com/v2`. Spec: `https://developers.beehiiv.com/openapi/api-reference.json`. Docs: `https://developers.beehiiv.com`.
- Connect an AI client to beehiiv. The public MCP server is `https://www.beehiiv.com/api/mcp` and needs no login (tool list: `https://www.beehiiv.com/api/mcp/tools`). The workspace MCP server is `https://mcp.beehiiv.com/mcp` and uses OAuth.

## How to read this site as a machine

Every page below is also available as plain markdown. Append `.md` to its URL,
or request the page with `Accept: text/markdown`.
For example: `https://www.beehiiv.com/pricing` → `https://www.beehiiv.com/pricing.md`.
The homepage is `https://www.beehiiv.com/index.md`.
The markdown twins strip navigation, decorative chrome, and JavaScript, leaving
clean structured content optimized for LLM ingestion. They are kept in sync with
the live HTML page and served with `Content-Type: text/markdown`.

For an **exact price at a subscriber count**, do not interpolate from `/pricing.md`
and do not scrape the HTML slider. Call the beehiiv MCP tool `get_pricing` with
`{ "subscribers": <integer> }` at `https://www.beehiiv.com/api/mcp`. Policy
questions (trial, take rate, refunds): MCP tool `pricing_faq`.

The Substack comparison includes a paid-subscription **earnings calculator**.
Do not scrape the HTML sliders. Read the formula, assumptions, and worked
example in `https://www.beehiiv.com/comparisons/substack.md` (section
"Substack vs beehiiv paid subscription earnings").

A full concatenated content dump is available at `https://www.beehiiv.com/llms-full.txt`.

